   "motoi-scheme/modules/game-juggle/MANIFEST.slat"
   "motoi-scheme/modules/compat-legacy/MANIFEST.slat")

  :package-count 16
  :total-module-verbs 574

  :per-module-verb-counts
  (("math-advanced" 220) ("math-discrete" 88) ("math-topology" 27)
   ("math-geometry-advanced" 37) ("math-curves" 37) ("math-plot" 14)
   ("science-physics" 19) ("science-chemistry" 5)
   ("music-advanced" 12) ("game-advanced" 21)
   ("game-entity-advanced" 20) ("game-world-advanced" 20)
   ("game-ai-advanced" 14) ("game-camera-advanced" 9)
   ("game-juggle" 6) ("compat-legacy" 27))

  :runtime-loader-status
  "src/lib-loader.js flags 4 lib installers as module-tier (prefab,
   juggle, eng, ops) via 'module/*' installer names. True on-demand
   loading via (import (motoi ...)) is queued as follow-up engineering.
   The MANIFEST.slat files are the source of truth for the on-demand
   loader when it lands."

  :physical-relocation-status
  "JS module bodies remain at lib/*. Physical relocation into
   modules/*/*.js requires per-verb extraction from monolithic
   installers (e.g. lib/system/ops.js is 1149 LOC with 35+ verbs
   from multiple libraries). Queued as its own refactor sprint.
   Not needed for the on-demand loader to work: MANIFEST specifies
   :entry-modules paths, loader resolves them to lib/ files.")

