;; ================================================================
;; NON-BLOCKING FOLLOW-UPS (for the next lane)
;; ================================================================

(follow-ups
  :queued
  ("Physical extraction of module-only verbs from monolithic lib installers
    (lib/system/ops.js is a 1149-LOC install-many-verbs file; splitting it
    into per-module .js files requires per-verb triage and shared-helper
    factoring)."

   "On-demand loader: implement (import (motoi <path>)) resolution against
    modules/<path>/MANIFEST.slat. Interpreter's import form currently no-ops
    for motoi paths."

   "Reference stripping of the 55 BUCKET-1 cruft records: mark each with
    :archived + :provenance-pointer per the Architect's disposition doctrine.
    The archive README enumerates which records get the flag."

   "Runtime implementation of the 259 declared-but-not-present CORE verbs.
    Pre-existing gap; not caused by this restructure but visible now that
    coreCoverage() surfaces it."

   "Per-module reference.slat authorship: extract verb records from
    MOTOI-SCHEME-REFERENCE.slat by :library tag into modules/<pkg>/reference.slat.
    Enables targeted RAG lookup per the Architect's TIER-7 pair-authoring plan."

   "Author dialect adapter for sakura's surface/* verbs so programs that
    #!dialect sakura get the surface/* implementations wired at load time."))

